{"event_type":"review","id":"24fc36fe2e56a198dad4286c1dfd87ac3624f4041d54f2fd5ece0e6927a03971","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T10:46:47Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/368710a2c614c928c39c3689a3832864d302aaba77330fcbc87f51e8edcee787","sha256":"368710a2c614c928c39c3689a3832864d302aaba77330fcbc87f51e8edcee787"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ff48a58179a976ac8d421d81862f5ae27e63b30edd73e6829bd24980a0113b65","sha256":"ff48a58179a976ac8d421d81862f5ae27e63b30edd73e6829bd24980a0113b65"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0f6ca071be724af7583580d8c00a5e2f488b64ec09150cfe94ea24c9a8252541","sha256":"0f6ca071be724af7583580d8c00a5e2f488b64ec09150cfe94ea24c9a8252541"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bfa7d57e40d562d192a03aeab5b9b48be4771d56372fe62c6365befe9b3adf6e","sha256":"bfa7d57e40d562d192a03aeab5b9b48be4771d56372fe62c6365befe9b3adf6e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/01c1adc50c3f22edb47e47621dda1ce95ac3f6cecfbed2e15bb4f872a028767e","sha256":"01c1adc50c3f22edb47e47621dda1ce95ac3f6cecfbed2e15bb4f872a028767e"}],"attempt_id":"46dcfd3b04ee7d273443f1253684f70a4314b5243bd55f74862e5a7bd1ac0ae9:0:1","base":"dea087931597968abfe84b55392d38ae56d19f5a","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"4bba45b75d7baa3afdb77c310f616956cccf125f","body":"**Use `PATCH` for the GitHub ref update.**\n\nThe GitHub REST update-reference endpoint uses `PATCH /repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/refs/{ref}`. `PUT` is not the update method, so this documented alternative will not perform the fast-forward update. Change `PUT` to `PATCH`. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/git/refs?apiVersion=2022-11-28&utm_source=openai))","id":"dc54a4262a7244d4f60ee0065a811c1552187813fb977645c9c1f069e880ecae","intervals":[],"path":"docs/drills/2026-09-h4.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use `PATCH` for the GitHub ref update."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"4bba45b75d7baa3afdb77c310f616956cccf125f","body":"**Resolve the parser explanation contradiction.**\n\nThe paragraph says that standard YAML parsers accept the scalar, then says `static: ` makes the same plain scalar invalid. These statements conflict. State which local tool accepted or normalized the value, and reserve “invalid” for the server-side parser result.","id":"93d06971e2af392a8daaa819a7dc30b8adeceaa2baf3cb896fa6857ea7f049ef","intervals":[],"path":"docs/drills/2026-09-h4.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Resolve the parser explanation contradiction."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"4bba45b75d7baa3afdb77c310f616956cccf125f","body":"**Do not enable force pushes on `main` for this drill.**\n\nThe drill force-pushes `refs/heads/merge-queue` at Line 36. `allow_force_pushes` on `main` does not enable that step and weakens the protected branch in the public scratch repository. Remove this setting or record an explicit rollback before leaving the repository in place.","id":"6d1d49cde9e7873307da38437991696678ba8a87f544906122a09854f505aec9","intervals":[],"path":"docs/drills/2026-09-h4.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not enable force pushes on `main` for this drill."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"26e205f6abce9aa55c43042fbb30ab780a3bdd0d","body":"**Make the `ratchet.yml` enforcement claims consistent.**\n\nLines 104-106 and 130-134 name `ratchet.yml` as a current required check. It drives `ratchet.checkRatchet` and `ratchet.monotonicGuard`. `policy/templates/README.md:20` describes the same file as \"LEGACY\" and \"retired at the ADR-0004 cutover\". Line 134 also cites the former local driver as deleted.\n\nReaders cannot tell which component enforces I5 today. Pick one status for `ratchet.yml`. Then align the README file table and the I4 and I5 enforcement text with it.\n\nAs per path instructions for `policy/**`: \"enforcement claims must name what actually enforces today.\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 130-134","id":"193511ac78f9f500b971662fb0c91a1e0f710cf9381f40f3a157ef7000b253f3","intervals":[],"path":"policy/DOCTRINE.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Make the `ratchet.yml` enforcement claims consistent."}],"head":"ee0f2eaec4c4931ed73501779776f715a38aa11c","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"e2f2233ab258a043a6c1f523b4cdc5940a56c06d","intervals":[[1,9]],"path":"baselines/typecheck--typecheck-count--7caef1e76077.json"},{"blob":"4bba45b75d7baa3afdb77c310f616956cccf125f","intervals":[[1,67]],"path":"docs/drills/2026-09-h4.md"},{"blob":"4e2c6f84eb1df3d1538683b0fbc0a829f7cb4f71","intervals":[[3,3],[5,8],[10,10],[22,23],[26,29],[31,42],[47,50],[53,54],[65,72],[74,74]],"path":"package.json"},{"blob":"26e205f6abce9aa55c43042fbb30ab780a3bdd0d","intervals":[[6,6],[10,11],[14,18],[32,32],[43,51],[65,75],[83,88],[104,106],[124,134],[196,197]],"path":"policy/DOCTRINE.md"},{"blob":"219811e37da29283cf36c4aed5198c58c7babfbc","intervals":[[11,34],[46,93],[102,102],[112,115],[119,121],[131,140],[142,149],[153,156],[165,166],[168,182],[188,225],[234,238]],"path":"policy/templates/README.md"},{"blob":"ade4f458fbcab54ca14d3d9cb7f7dd4b4f546024","intervals":[[2,24],[26,32],[34,55],[57,57],[59,63],[65,68],[70,94]],"path":"scripts/ratchet-typecheck.mjs"},{"blob":"365ba21d9fb3f4eed7f0525df3375ed58217726c","intervals":[[1,502]],"path":"test/fixtures/ratchet-lib-selfhost.mjs"},{"blob":"760682ad9acb33c5d113aac27e9e16b89858810d","intervals":[[3,7],[15,15],[18,22],[29,35],[45,45],[49,53],[55,61],[66,66],[68,69],[78,78],[84,87],[92,96],[108,108],[123,125],[127,147]],"path":"test/scripts/demo-eval-axes.test.ts"}],"job_id":"46dcfd3b04ee7d273443f1253684f70a4314b5243bd55f74862e5a7bd1